      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "a square piece; a slice of bread, cheese, or cake",
      "evidence": [
        "Mart. 12.32.18: <span lang=\"la\">Nec quadra deerat cāseī Tolōsātis</span>",
        "Hor. Ep. 1.17.49: <span lang=\"la\">dīviduō findētur mūnere quadra</span>",
        "Sen. Ben. 4.29.2: <span lang=\"la\">quadra pānis</span> (Lewis &amp; Short)",
        "M-O s.v. slice: <span lang=\"la\">quadra</span>, if square, as a slice of bread"
      ],
      "comment": "A piece cut from a round loaf scored into sections, or from a cheese or a cake. Vergil’s Trojans eat even the <span lang=\"la\">quadrae</span> of bread they had used as plates (A. 7.115), and <span lang=\"la\">alienā vīvere quadrā</span> is to live off another man’s table (Juv. 5.2)."
    }
